## How to Deploy to your cPanel (`editians.sanviraj.com`)

Since you wanted to host this on your cPanel, I have pre-built the entire React application into static files. No server setup is required!

1. Open the File Explorer on your computer and navigate to:
   `C:\Users\User\.gemini\antigravity\scratch\Editians Hub\editians-chat\dist`

   **Note:** The `dist` folder contains your production-ready website!

2. Log in to your **cPanel**.
3. Open the **File Manager**.
4. Navigate to the folder for your subdomain (e.g., `public_html/editians` or wherever `editians.sanviraj.com` points to).
5. **Upload everything** inside your local `dist` folder into that cPanel folder.
   *(Make sure you upload the `index.html` and the `assets` folder directly into the root of the subdomain folder).*

### Important Setup Step for cPanel (React Router)
Because it's a React "Single Page Application", if a user tries to access `/chat` directly, cPanel might throw a 404 error. To fix this, create a `.htaccess` file in that same folder on cPanel and paste this inside:

```apache
<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
  RewriteEngine On
  RewriteBase /
  RewriteRule ^index\.html$ - [L]
  RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-f
  RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-d
  RewriteRule . /index.html [L]
</IfModule>
```

That's it! Your entire real-time, anonymous chat platform is ready.
